# Response headers for Cloudflare Pages and Netlify (both read this file).
# GitHub Pages ignores it - it cannot set custom headers at all, which is one
# more reason this site is deployed elsewhere.
#
# These are defence in depth. The Content-Security-Policy inside each page's
# <meta> tag already carries the load-bearing rules; frame-ancestors is the one
# directive a meta tag cannot express, so it has to live here.

/*
  Content-Security-Policy: frame-ancestors 'none'
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: no-referrer
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=(), usb=(), payment=()

# Deliberately NOT set: Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy. Enabling it would block
# the cross-origin <img> loads that "Add from a web address" depends on.
